<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103443" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρά̆-μηνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of four months, lasting four months</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.63
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράμηνοι ὀχεύουσι</span>
			<i>at four months old</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				545b1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράμηνον</span>
			<i>for a space of four months</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				573a13
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				291
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				498
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πρώτη
			τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				410.4
			</span></i> (Erythrae, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>); so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράμηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aph.</u>
					4.1
				</span></i>
			: 
				Boeot.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετράμεινος</span> (q.v.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
